{
 "item": "03",
 "title": "Concentric cylinders: D against m for three K, with the slip-form rule",
 "status": "final (rc2 runs) for g <= 200 dx; the rows at g = 400 dx are not reached",
 "caption": "Relative change D of the torque between concentric cylinders (R1 = 4 g, R2 = 5 g, w = 0 on both walls) against m = g / (2 l) for K = 3, 1 and 0.5 (Re = 10 on mu_inf; 25, 15 and 12.5 on mu; Ma = 0.02). (a) Exact solution (solid), the wall rule in its slip form (dashed; every wall displaced by delta = K l / (2 (1 + K)) into the fluid, the rotor's apparent speed reduced by 2 delta Omega) and the runs (points; bars: noise floor of D from three lattices, smaller than the symbols). (b) The same as ratios to the exact value; the rule leaves the frame below m of about 1.9 (1.36 to 1.49 at m = 1). Resolution of the rows (m, l / dx, g / dx): (1, 50, 100), (2, 25, 100), (5, 10, 100), (10, 10, 200), (20, 5, 200). Runs: the sweep rows of tab_04; tag `thesis-ch5-rc2`, `thesis-ch5-rc2-3-g656e652`, `thesis-ch5-rc2-6-gaa27df9`, `thesis-ch5-rc2-2-g7a21ef4`, `thesis-ch5-rc2-1-gcb243fd`. Ratio to exact: m = 1: runs 1.000 to 1.001, rule 1.365 to 1.487; m = 2: runs 1.001 to 1.001, rule 1.035 to 1.039; m = 5: runs 1.005 to 1.007, rule 0.997 to 0.997; m = 10: runs 1.006 to 1.008, rule 0.999 to 0.999; m = 20: runs 1.024 to 1.032, rule 0.999 to 0.999.",
